From 0f05d9642063cdaf4d7ce991e3781be893b9ca04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:49:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wallet(v2): receive explicit native keyhash payments with
 truthful ownership

Add getnewaddress(label, "native") without changing legacy/default receiving. Native address payloads stay distinct from legacy key and script IDs, persist through the existing addressbook encoding, and resolve only the exact canonical native keyhash policy to wallet keys. Preserve immutable native wire bytes while reporting receiving addresses, labels, watch-only ownership and transaction history. Reject unsupported legacy script construction and ordinary native funding rather than converting policy languages. Ordinary native coin spendability remains false.

Before proof: the exact immutable pool daemon rejects the new explicit native address argument with RPC -1; raw evidence is in native-wallet-receive/before.log. New unit and lifecycle tests cover ownership, real native payout maturity/signatures, wrong keys, labels, restart/rescan/reorg, locked/public-only/descriptor controls. Normal build and after tests pending; no broader validation claim.
